---
description: Booking user-facing copy must live in client/server bookingMessages catalogs, not inline in components or controllers.
alwaysApply: true
---

# Booking user-visible messages

Whenever you add or change **text that end users see** for the booking flow (UI labels, validation, toasts, dialogs, calendar strings, API error bodies users read, booking-related domain errors, booking emails), **do not** leave long literals scattered in components or controllers.

## Where to put copy

| Layer | File |
|-------|------|
| React client (pages, components, hooks) | `client/src/messages/bookingMessages.jsx` (edit here). `bookingMessages.js` only re-exports so `.js` importers resolve under Vite. |
| Express (controllers, services, rules, notifications) | `server/messages/bookingMessages.js` — **no JSX**; strings or `(params) => string` with a **single object** for parameterized helpers. `api` = HTTP JSON; `domain` = rule errors; `email` = HTML (`title` + `body`, subjects like `subject: ({ id }) => …`). |

1. Add a **descriptive key** (or small nested object) in the appropriate section of the right file (e.g. `bookingForm.fields.*`, `calendar.legend.*`, `api.*`, `email.*`).
2. **Import** the catalog in the file that needs the string and reference the key.
3. Keep **dynamic** phrases as functions that take parameters (see existing `conflictLine`, `errorLoading`, etc.).

## Client catalog shape (`bookingMessages.jsx`)

- **`myBookings.activeCard.alerts`** — contention / on-hold notices: `icon`, `title` / `body`, optional `introInSingleParagraph`, parameterized lines (`challengingLine({ bookingId, timeRange, email })`, …), toggle **strings** for aria.
- **`myBookings.activeCard.meta`** — inline card copy: `purposeLabel()`, `previousAttempts.label({ count })`, `bookingLine({ id, statusLabel })`, etc.
- **`myBookings.activeCard.convertPanel`** — convert-to-firm UI: `icons.convertError`, JSX functions for labels/help, **plain string** only for `convertPurposePlaceholder` (HTML `placeholder` attr).
- **`bookingForm`** — `schema` / `docErrors` / `apiFallbacks` / `convertFirmDefaultSuccess` stay **plain strings** (Zod, errors, session). `labels.bookingType` stays string map. `fields.resourceFallback`, `resourceNumber`, and all `*Placeholder` / `selectRoom` text stay **strings**. Everything else is **`() => ReactNode`** or **`({ ... }) => ReactNode`** (e.g. `formCard.conflictLine({ id, resourceName, typeLabel, statusLabel, range })`).
- **`calendar`** — `legend` / `flyout` visible copy: JSX functions; `flyout.ariaDialog` and `event.expandOverlap*` stay **strings** (aria/title attrs). `fetchAvailabilityFailed`, `aggregateMonthTitle({ … })` (string title), `errorLoading({ message })`, `hover`, `roleLabel` stay **string**-based for tooltips/utils.

Do **not** use `dangerouslySetInnerHTML`; use JSX fragments (or plain strings where required above).

## Out of scope

- **Non-booking** features should use a **separate** messages module if you introduce them (same pattern: one client + one server file per domain if both layers show copy).
- **Developer-only** strings (`console.error`, internal assert messages, comments) do not need to go in these catalogs.
- **Swagger / OpenAPI** descriptions live in `server/docs/swagger.json` unless the same sentence is shown in the app UI—then duplicate or derive carefully.

If you touch booking UX copy, default to **extending these two files** before adding new inline user-facing strings elsewhere.
